# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JBC Skin Cream App — list of settings the app needs
# This file is PUBLISHED to GitHub. Never put a real secret here.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the real values there.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Phase 2: Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ──────────────────────
# Neon Console → your project → Connection Details → Pooled connection.
# Copy the "postgresql://..." string.
#
# IMPORTANT: use the POOLED connection string, not the direct one. The
# pooled one is the one that works on serverless hosting like Vercel.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# ── Phase 2: Sign-in (Better Auth) ───────────────────────────
# Sign-in needs a secret that only this app knows. It signs the session
# cookies, so anyone who has it can sign in as your users.
#
# Generate one by running:  openssl rand -base64 32
# Or paste this in your terminal and use the result:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="paste-a-long-random-string-here"

# The address Better Auth is running at. Must match NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Phase 2: Google sign-in ──────────────────────────────────
# From Google Cloud Console → your project → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# OAuth 2.0 Client ID.
#
# You need these because Better Auth talks to Google directly. VibeKit uses
# Neon + Better Auth, not Supabase, so Google has to be set up by hand.
#
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── Phase 4: Admin allowlist ──────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated email addresses allowed to open the admin page.
# Anyone not on this list is refused, even if they sign in with Google.
# CHANGE THIS before going live. It should never stay as the example below.
# Format: first@example.com,second@example.com
ADMIN_EMAILS="admin@example.com"

# ── Optional: Upstash Redis cache ────────────────────────────
# Speeds up the "my requests" list so the database is not queried
# on every visit. Leave BOTH blank and the app still works, just
# without the cache — nothing breaks.
# Create a free database at upstash.com → Console → Create → Redis.
# Copy the REST URL and the REST token.
UPSTASH_REDIS_URL=""
UPSTASH_REDIS_TOKEN=""

# ── Not required by JBC ──────────────────────────────────────
# JBC has no online payment, no file uploads and no email sending,
# so those keys are deliberately absent.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=""         # Only needed if you later email clients
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""      # Not used — payment is out of scope for v1
